==========================================================================
  ARM DECISION — the two criteria, side by side
==========================================================================

  1. readout-efficiency gap at 'l2' (smaller is better — a large gap means the readout, not the code, is what the perturbation is measuring)
       delay     +0.011
       nodelay   +0.218
     -> favours delay

  2. |b_a(usage) - b_a(control)| at 'l2' (larger is better — the timing probe has to be distinguishable from a pure rate insult)
       delay     +0.0744
       nodelay   -0.0364
     -> favours delay

  Both were measured at layer 1 only in document 5 and are NOT inherited here (document 7 §5 step 2).
  Record the decision in the progress document; it is not made by this script.

